      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Federated Profile Claims**\n\nI'm focusing on creating a `profile_claims.py` file to handle federated user profile data. Right now, I'm thinking about Google as a concrete external provider for federated login. This will be the basis for fetching and normalizing claims. I'll need to ensure the provider is clearly identifiable within the code for clarity and maintainability.\n\n\n**Constructing `profile_claims.py`**\n\nI'm making headway on `profile_claims.py`. The focus is on fetching and normalizing profile claims, with Google as the initial provider. I have outlined a plan to create a function that takes an access token, simulates an HTTP request to the Google UserInfo API endpoint, and parses the JSON response into normalized claims. The Google API endpoint will be clearly marked in the code. I'll be working on simulating the external call.\n\n\n",
