      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Callback Implementation**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up the groundwork to generate a Python script named `oauth_callback.py`. This script will be the critical handler for the OAuth/OIDC callback. The main job is to exchange an authorization code to access the tokens. I've decided to proceed using Auth0 as the external provider, making it the definitive external provider to work with.\n\n\n**Constructing Core Functionality**\n\nI'm now outlining the `oauth_callback.py` structure. It'll start with imports for `os` and `requests`. I'll define environment variables for Auth0 configuration. A function, `handle_oauth_callback`, will handle the authorization code exchange, making a POST request to Auth0's token endpoint. This should return the tokens. I'll use the `write` tool to set up the file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866923592,
          "start": 1789866920614
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc61caa600163bWFgKCeFE4zy",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc61c56a001x0c3Va87BvPze6",
      "session_id": "ses_f439e3aa8ffePpKikYoDoAHO53",
      "time_created": 1789866920614,
      "time_updated": 1789866923592
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tsgslbUpyDo5dlVe",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport requests\nimport json\n\nAUTH0_DOMAIN = os.getenv(\"AUTH0_DOMAIN\")\nAUTH0_CLIENT_ID = os.getenv(\"AUTH0_CLIENT_ID\")\nAUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET = os.getenv(\"AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET\")\nAUTH0_CALLBACK_URL = os.getenv(\"AUTH0_CALLBACK_URL\")\n\ndef handle_oauth_callback(authorization_code: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles the OAuth/OIDC callback and exchanges an authorization code for tokens.\n\n    Args:\n        authorization_code: The authorization code received from the identity provider.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary containing the access, ID, and refresh tokens.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not all([AUTH0_DOMAIN, AUTH0_CLIENT_ID, AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET, AUTH0_CALLBACK_URL]):\n        raise ValueError(\"Auth0 environment variables not set.\")\n\n    token_url = f\"https://{AUTH0_DOMAIN}/oauth/token\"\n    headers = {\"content-type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"}\n    payload = {\n        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n        \"client_id\": AUTH0_CLIENT_ID,\n        \"client_secret\": AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET,\n        \"code\": authorization_code,\n        \"redirect_uri\": AUTH0_CALLBACK_URL,\n    }\n\n    try:\n        response = requests.post(token_url, headers=headers, data=payload)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n        tokens = response.json()\n        return {\n            \"access_token\": tokens.get(\"access_token\"),\n            \"id_token\": tokens.get(\"id_token\"),\n            \"refresh_token\": tokens.get(\"refresh_token\"),\n            \"expires_in\": tokens.get(\"expires_in\")\n        }\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        print(f\"Error exchanging authorization code for tokens: {e}\")\n        raise\n\n",
            "filePath": "oauth_callback.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
