      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Google as Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google as the initial external provider for this OAuth/OIDC login flow. I'm focusing on creating the `start_oauth_login.py` script now, and this choice gives me a well-documented starting point.\n\n\n**Constructing Authorization URL**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in building `start_oauth_login.py`. I've outlined the necessary components: the Google OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint and the key parameters such as client ID, redirect URI, scope, and response type. I intend to hardcode these values as placeholders for now, anticipating their eventual sourcing from environment variables or a configuration file. The code will generate the authorization URL for redirection.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866918323,
          "start": 1789866915990
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc61b896001LT05F21ZmSLtdf",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc61b35000173mPJ5egI6ZBfw",
